+
+```text
+Recommendations 
+ 
+1. FAA should correct its response to th e Commission’s May 22, 2003, Question for 
+the Record. 
+ 
+2. FAA should consider appr opriate administrative action for the two current 
+executives who did not act to correct th e record with the Commission.  In our 
+view, they had an affirmative obligati on to do so in light of the Commission’s 
+mandate that included examining, and accurately reporting on, the interaction 
+between FAA and DOD on Sept ember 11.  The time at which the Air Force 
+Liaison joined the FAA headquarters phone -bridge and established contact with 
+NORAD was relevant to the Commission’s mandate. 
+ 
+As a mitigating factor, and to provide some  context, we note th at at the time, the 
+FAA, including these executives, produced over 6,000 documents and materials   
+to the Commission.
+```
